      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e6f2595d",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "intended audience",
      "description": "The meme is designed for an audience that may be familiar with or receptive to inflammatory stereotypes about Muslims or people from the Middle East, particularly those who might find humor in or be desensitized to hate speech. The target community likely includes individuals who are exposed to or propagate Islamophobic rhetoric, and who may interpret the meme as a joke or a provocative statement rather than a hateful generalization. The meme’s visual and textual elements are crafted to appeal to those who understand the symbolic association between camels and the Middle East, and who may be inclined to accept or spread the false equivalence between camels (as symbols) and terrorism.",
